# Apli.ai client - build-time settings.
#
# Copy to `.env` only if you need to change something. The defaults are right
# for every normal deployment, which is why this file is almost empty.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# TWO THINGS TO KNOW
#
# 1. These are read when you run `npm run build`, not when the app runs. The
#    values are compiled into the bundle, so changing one means building
#    again and republishing.
#
# 2. Everything here ships to the browser and is readable by anyone who opens
#    devtools. Only `VITE_`-prefixed names are exposed at all, and none of
#    them may be a secret. API keys and passwords belong in the server's .env.

# Where the API is.
#
# Leave it unset. The default is the relative path `/api`, which means "the
# same origin that served this page" - and one origin is what lets the
# session cookie work without CORS having to be right.
#
# Set it only when the client is deployed somewhere the API is not: a CDN, a
# separate host, a different port. If you do, two things follow:
#   - the server's CLIENT_ORIGIN must name this client's exact address, and
#   - over plain http a browser will still refuse the `secure` session cookie,
#     so COOKIE_SECURE has to stay false until there is a certificate.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com/api
